            "review_title": "Review at Purple Log",
            "review_text": "Grace F\nAdelaide, Australia13 contributions\n0\nDisappointing\nJan 2019 • Couples\nWe were visiting here on our last day in Ho Chi Minh(we are from Australia). This was supposed to be our last Vietnamese meal for the trip...\nThe Pho was tasteless and the portion size was small. We’ve had a lot of Pho in Vietnam and the soup part of the dish had minimal flavor, neither of us finished our dishes. We also ordered fresh Vietnamese rolls...These came out after we had finished our Pho- we had to wait around 25 minutes. When they arrived the dish was not what we ordered. It was pan fried tofu or fish, we weren’t entirely sure. It was rubbery and basically inedible. \nThe location and set up is lovely but it was a disappointing final meal for us. The staff were lovely but English was limited which made it difficult to convey our issues.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten January 6, 2019",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
